 # P2P distribution integration
 
 The P2P repository tracks `Ryu7w7/OCTR-NitroFueled-PC` releases with a separately
-licensed adapter recipe. This integration is based on upstream `v0.7.5`
-(`3885d1aea24d19ed9b31f96fba57a5cce92183cd`). The original contributor identities,
+licensed adapter recipe. This integration is based on upstream `v0.8.3`
+(`418940a6635afe3aeeed8f0d286358319c935a44`). The original contributor identities,
 GPL-2.0-or-later license, and third-party notices remain applicable.
 
 The integration preserves the upstream mod/restart fixes and RyuNET clock,
 request-form and ping support. External PSN publishers keep their original
-URL/Host requests without RyuNET proofs, inventory headers, retry forms or clock
+URL/Host requests without RyuNET proofs, inventory/client headers, retry forms or clock
 updates. The Room panel directs external-backend players to the game lobby;
 it does not interpret RyuNET ping state as a Steam room. HTTP loopback fixtures,
 launcher fixtures and the independent socket-policy matrix cover these boundaries.
 
-The v0.7.5 integration also keeps RyuNET itemless/private-cup coordination and
-its native mode callbacks disabled for external backends. Local performance
+The v0.8.3 integration keeps RyuNET Itemless, private-cup/team coordination,
+AI reference preparation and their native mode callbacks disabled for external
+backends. RyuNET HTTP sessions, machine fingerprint collection, chat, spectator
+sharing, name-color polling and room verification stay inactive. Inherited
+RyuNET client metadata and item-rule capabilities are cleared before launch;
+independent mod file maps remain intact. Local performance
 reports remain available, but are never uploaded to RyuNET or the external
 publisher, even when an existing profile enables upstream reporting. The
 upstream renderer, local mod preparation and default RyuNET behavior are retained.
